#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# doc: migrated from tests/fixtures/none_literal_at_call_arg_resource.gg (run_gg pair)
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "5\nnone\nsome hi\n"
#!end
# Sibling of `none_literal_at_call_arg.gg`, which covers Option[int] — a
# PRIMITIVE payload that is never Ptr-wrapped at a bare param, so it cannot
# reach this bug. This fixture exercises the RESOURCE-payload shape:
# `Option[String]` appears as a struct field, which registers it in the
# self-host lowerer's `optionlike_resource_types`, so `lower_function`
# Ptr-wraps the bare `Option[String]` param (by-pointer ABI). The wrapped
# tid is what `GirFunction.param_types` records; without peeling it back to
# the VALUE type at the call-arg expected-type writer, a bare `None` arg
# types its dst local as the Ptr tid → scalar LIR slot → the prelude-variant
# intercept falls back → cc-invalid `(Option__T){.tag=1}` assigned into an
# int64 temp (the lower.gg-split's stage-1 cc failure, 146 sites).
#
# The callee is textually BEFORE the caller on purpose: the forward-callee
# shape is a separate latent class (see none_literal_forward_callee.gg).

public struct Tag:
    Option[String] label

int check(Option[String] o):
    match o:
        case Some(s):
            return s.len()
        case None:
            return 5

String describe(Option[String] o):
    match o:
        case Some(s):
            return f"some {s}"
        case None:
            return "none"

void main():
    print(check(None))
    print(describe(None))
    print(describe(Some("hi")))
